    "title": "pandas.Series.dt.hour — pandas 3.0.5 documentation",
    "status": 200,
    "markdown": "# pandas.Series.dt.hour#\n\n- Series.dt.hour[source]#\n- The hours of the datetime. See also \n  - `DatetimeIndex.day`\n  - The day of the datetime.\n  - `DatetimeIndex.minute`\n  - The minutes of the datetime.\n  - `DatetimeIndex.second`\n  - The seconds of the datetime.\n Examples >>> datetime_series = pd.Series( ... pd.date_range(\"2000-01-01\", periods=3, freq=\"h\") ... ) >>> datetime_series 0 2000-01-01 00:00:00 1 2000-01-01 01:00:00 2 2000-01-01 02:00:00 dtype: datetime64[us] >>> datetime_series.dt.hour 0 0 1 1 2 2 dtype: int32",
